# Lucy in the Sky with Diamonds, refrain (figure 108.4)
# Seven bars: the two-bar phrase three times, then a bar of D (V in G, IV in A) leading to the
# verse's A. The "A 2 3" typed for the verse's first bar is its 3/4 count.
#? The verse's 3/4 bar is drawn 3 beats long; if the refrain's quarter is two verse beats (as in
#? the bridge, fig. 108.3), it should sound as 1.5 refrain beats. Check against the record.
meter 4/4
key G

system
chords   | [3X] G{I} C{IV} | D{V} |

system
chords   | D{V = A: IV} | [Verse] <3> A{A: I} |
words    | r | <3> 1 2 3 |
